(4135974, 594904, 34618, '<td valign="top">IHMO you should have left in the top and left-hand edges of the fan, or cut them out much more. As it is they look like you just missed giving them enough room to be in the frame. Not sure what you were doing with the color/color balance, but the tone isn''t really sepia and isn''t proper balance, so seems a bit confusing, too. The background detracts a bit, too. There''s some shelf or something at the top that has a shadow that breaks the concentricity of the fan. The pole or whatever is coming up out of the back also leads your eye away from a smooth track.  Hope that''s helpful and not too jarring.</td>', 'IHMO you should have left in the top and left-hand edges of the fan, or cut them out much more. As it is they look like you just missed giving them enough room to be in the frame. Not sure what you were doing with the color/color balance, but the tone isn''t really sepia and isn''t proper balance, so seems a bit confusing, too. The background detracts a bit, too. There''s some shelf or something at the top that has a shadow that breaks the concentricity of the fan. The pole or whatever is coming up out of the back also leads your eye away from a smooth track.  Hope that''s helpful and not too jarring.', '2007-10-03 02:23:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4135975, 594806, 3727, '<td valign="top">made me laugh... i actually have 6 remotes lol (sat radio, tv, vcr, dvd, stereo x 2 ). All old so don''t work with each other and can''t bring myself to go buy one of those 100 buck remotes that do it all lol</td>', 'made me laugh... i actually have 6 remotes lol (sat radio, tv, vcr, dvd, stereo x 2 ). All old so don''t work with each other and can''t bring myself to go buy one of those 100 buck remotes that do it all lol', '2007-10-03 02:24:09.000000', NULL, 1),
