(4156729, 594506, 83590, '<td valign="top">It''s a 74LS14 Hex Schmidt Trigger Inverter sitting in a Banksia flower, lit overhead by a 430EX with a Stofen.<br/> <br/>You know, I spent hours agonising over this challenge. Drove all over the country side trying to find something worth shooting, with no luck. I had bought my wife a native flower bouquet earlier, and I stood there looking at it one night, and thought I might as well do a "bugshot" :)<br/> <br/>I really like how the flower petals look like they''re inspecting this hi-tech foreign intruder. I also didn''t notice the little green eyes on the IC until I uploaded the pictures.<br/> <br/>Thank you all for your comments and votes!</td>', 'It''s a 74LS14 Hex Schmidt Trigger Inverter sitting in a Banksia flower, lit overhead by a 430EX with a Stofen. You know, I spent hours agonising over this challenge. Drove all over the country side trying to find something worth shooting, with no luck. I had bought my wife a native flower bouquet earlier, and I stood there looking at it one night, and thought I might as well do a "bugshot" :) I really like how the flower petals look like they''re inspecting this hi-tech foreign intruder. I also didn''t notice the little green eyes on the IC until I uploaded the pictures. Thank you all for your comments and votes!', '2007-10-10 07:21:56.000000', NULL, 0),
