(4157130, 594506, 28710, '<td valign="top">very nicely controlled reds in a difficult situation with low contrast, high saturation color. <br/> <br/>To my eye, I''m seeing a fair bit of oversharpening artifacts where the red meets the green.<br/> <br/>My best guess is that these were introduced as a part of the resizing for web procedure. May I suggest using a bit of a mask on your sharpening layer, specifically on BG/bokeh areas and high contrast edges.</td>', 'very nicely controlled reds in a difficult situation with low contrast, high saturation color.  To my eye, I''m seeing a fair bit of oversharpening artifacts where the red meets the green. My best guess is that these were introduced as a part of the resizing for web procedure. May I suggest using a bit of a mask on your sharpening layer, specifically on BG/bokeh areas and high contrast edges.', '2007-10-10 10:57:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4157134, 594686, 28710, '<td valign="top">I''m really digging the tones you use in your skies in many of the images in your portfolio.</td>', 'I''m really digging the tones you use in your skies in many of the images in your portfolio.', '2007-10-10 10:58:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4157162, 594273, 80952, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Nowhere_Man:</b></div><hr/><i> I like the concept but the image itself is somewhat uninspired.  Somewhat lacking in contrast, a little too much sharpening, a little noisy.  The way the top of the calculator and the bottom of the bill just barely extends past the frame is bothering me- it''s like the crop was left to chance, not deliberate enough.  Sorry for being so harsh, hope it''s at least somewhat helpful.  I hate it when my images get low votes with no explanation. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Tks for the comments. It''s very helpfull to find out where i''m wrong especialy that i''m a begginer in photography. Tks a lot.</td>', 'Originally posted by Nowhere_Man: I like the concept but the image itself is somewhat uninspired.  Somewhat lacking in contrast, a little too much sharpening, a little noisy.  The way the top of the calculator and the bottom of the bill just barely extends past the frame is bothering me- it''s like the crop was left to chance, not deliberate enough.  Sorry for being so harsh, hope it''s at least somewhat helpful.  I hate it when my images get low votes with no explanation.   Tks for the comments. It''s very helpfull to find out where i''m wrong especialy that i''m a begginer in photography. Tks a lot.', '2007-10-10 11:04:49.000000', NULL, 0),
