(4163123, 593479, 49109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by unknowndeath:</b></div><hr/><i> What the hell is it? What does it mean why did you shoot it? I am stunned and not so greatly I just don''t fucking get it. bubbles and machines hmm...explain it to me I am stupid! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is a hard disk with water droplets. I does mean nothing to me personally, but I thought it was a good way to illustrate technology. You might want to look up "overflow" in the dictionary, you''ll surely get the connection. )Oh wait, I did it for you:<br/> <br/>overflow: noun<br/>...3 Computing: the generation of a number or some other data item that is too large for an assigned location or memory space<br/> <br/>got it?</td>', 'Originally posted by unknowndeath: What the hell is it? What does it mean why did you shoot it? I am stunned and not so greatly I just don''t fucking get it. bubbles and machines hmm...explain it to me I am stupid!   This is a hard disk with water droplets. I does mean nothing to me personally, but I thought it was a good way to illustrate technology. You might want to look up "overflow" in the dictionary, you''ll surely get the connection. )Oh wait, I did it for you: overflow: noun...3 Computing: the generation of a number or some other data item that is too large for an assigned location or memory space got it?', '2007-10-12 15:14:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4163779, 593479, 70000, '<td valign="top">Your focus and lighting are very good and it fits the challenge, it is aesthetically pleasing as well but after unknowndeath''s question it does me me wonder a bit why there are water droplets on a hard disk, still congrats on your ribbon :)</td>', 'Your focus and lighting are very good and it fits the challenge, it is aesthetically pleasing as well but after unknowndeath''s question it does me me wonder a bit why there are water droplets on a hard disk, still congrats on your ribbon :)', '2007-10-12 20:55:50.000000', NULL, 0),
