(4169178, 592194, 79604, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image of the bridge Joe! Lighting is great. I was at that same spot last Wednesday. The sky and clouds were gorgeous...I went to take a pic and my batteries died...with no spares in sight :(<br/>Congratulations on a strong finish. Well deserved.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-15 12:36:38.</i></td>', 'Beautiful image of the bridge Joe! Lighting is great. I was at that same spot last Wednesday. The sky and clouds were gorgeous...I went to take a pic and my batteries died...with no spares in sight :(Congratulations on a strong finish. Well deserved.', '2007-10-15 13:34:34.000000', '2007-10-15 13:36:38.000000', 0),
(4170963, 592289, 39427, '<td valign="top">aw, sad to see this got the DQ... what happened?</td>', 'aw, sad to see this got the DQ... what happened?', '2007-10-16 02:24:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4172737, 594880, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Hi my name is Leroy. I am here in response to your request for an indepth critique of this photo.<br/> <br/><b>First Reaction (the most important one)</b> <br/>Technically a good photo, but overall a tad boring.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting</b> <br/>Lighting is excellent. You''ve done what I assume you intended masterfully here.<br/> <br/><b>Composition</b> <br/>Ehh, it''s ok for a product image. Nothing special though.<br/> <br/><b>Focus and other Technicals</b> <br/>As I mentioned earlier, technicals are strong. Exposure is right on, focus is sharp, lighting is good. Nice work.<br/> <br/><b>Meeting the Challenge</b> <br/>Definitely meets the challenge, although in a way that doesn''t really stand out.<br/> <br/><b>How to grow its score</b> <br/>As you likely know, DPC responds well to WOW,no wow means mediocre scores. It''s sort of a shame, but that''s the way it goes here.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion</b> <br/>Technically a good image, would do well as stock. <br/> <br/>This critique is strictly my opinion based on observations of this photo. If you have any questions feel free to contact me through the DPC PM system.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from Critique Club  Hi my name is Leroy. I am here in response to your request for an indepth critique of this photo. First Reaction (the most important one) Technically a good photo, but overall a tad boring. Lighting Lighting is excellent. You''ve done what I assume you intended masterfully here. Composition Ehh, it''s ok for a product image. Nothing special though. Focus and other Technicals As I mentioned earlier, technicals are strong. Exposure is right on, focus is sharp, lighting is good. Nice work. Meeting the Challenge Definitely meets the challenge, although in a way that doesn''t really stand out. How to grow its score As you likely know, DPC responds well to WOW,no wow means mediocre scores. It''s sort of a shame, but that''s the way it goes here. Conclusion Technically a good image, would do well as stock.  This critique is strictly my opinion based on observations of this photo. If you have any questions feel free to contact me through the DPC PM system.', '2007-10-16 21:28:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4172933, 593249, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Hi my name is Leroy. I am here in response to your request for an indepth critique of this photo.<br/> <br/><b>First Reaction (the most important one)</b> <br/>I''m usually pretty liberal on if things meet the challenge, and I couldn''t force myself to make this one fit.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting</b> <br/>Lighting is a bit boring and overall just flat. <br/> <br/><b>Composition</b> <br/>For this type of shot, I suppose the composition is ok, but nothing really makes it stand out.<br/> <br/><b>Focus and other Technicals</b> <br/>Focus seems ok, exposure is also ok. May be just a tad overexposed.<br/> <br/><b>Meeting the Challenge</b> <br/>Not even close. Now, if it had been smoke and mirrors, I might have given it to ya :-)<br/> <br/><b>How to grow its score</b> <br/>DPC loves pizazz and wow, but most of all they like images to meet the challenge.<br/> <br/><b>Conclusion</b> <br/>Keep working at it. Most of all, enjoy what ya shoot and do it for you. The rest will come with time.<br/> <br/>This critique is strictly my opinion based on observations of this photo. If you have any questions feel free to contact me through the DPC PM system.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from Critique Club  Hi my name is Leroy. I am here in response to your request for an indepth critique of this photo. First Reaction (the most important one) I''m usually pretty liberal on if things meet the challenge, and I couldn''t force myself to make this one fit. Lighting Lighting is a bit boring and overall just flat.  Composition For this type of shot, I suppose the composition is ok, but nothing really makes it stand out. Focus and other Technicals Focus seems ok, exposure is also ok. May be just a tad overexposed. Meeting the Challenge Not even close. Now, if it had been smoke and mirrors, I might have given it to ya :-) How to grow its score DPC loves pizazz and wow, but most of all they like images to meet the challenge. Conclusion Keep working at it. Most of all, enjoy what ya shoot and do it for you. The rest will come with time. This critique is strictly my opinion based on observations of this photo. If you have any questions feel free to contact me through the DPC PM system.', '2007-10-16 22:56:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4172955, 594887, 46336, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club. </b> <br/> <br/>Hi Dave, <br/> <br/>Well, you got a bunch of really positive comments, as well as a mass of votes in 4/5 space. A 7.57 avg for commenators is pretty good. You really hit a cord with a few people, but not many. Not much below, and with good reason - there isn;t much to dislike. <br/> <br/>Its an interesting take to critique - as my eye moves over I personally pass from being really engaged to not very interested at all. Lets consider this. The subject and foreground is superb - there is a sense of movement, and action, and power - lovely lines and swirling dust. Would have liked to see more of the workers face - maybe with soem sweat and a grimace, but understand that you couldn''t engineer these things. The near-background of the cars, especially the blow-out on the hood is an annoying distraction, and the far-bacvkground is a lto of negative space that doesn''t really add value. I think you got a positive reponse from those who dwelt on your foreground and subject.<br/> <br/>What could make this a better image? Not too much considerign the circumstances it was made in. Fo mysefl I would have cropped the top off, and tried to burn the hood of the car and the pole. <br/> <br/>It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Paul</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.   Hi Dave,  Well, you got a bunch of really positive comments, as well as a mass of votes in 4/5 space. A 7.57 avg for commenators is pretty good. You really hit a cord with a few people, but not many. Not much below, and with good reason - there isn;t much to dislike.  Its an interesting take to critique - as my eye moves over I personally pass from being really engaged to not very interested at all. Lets consider this. The subject and foreground is superb - there is a sense of movement, and action, and power - lovely lines and swirling dust. Would have liked to see more of the workers face - maybe with soem sweat and a grimace, but understand that you couldn''t engineer these things. The near-background of the cars, especially the blow-out on the hood is an annoying distraction, and the far-bacvkground is a lto of negative space that doesn''t really add value. I think you got a positive reponse from those who dwelt on your foreground and subject. What could make this a better image? Not too much considerign the circumstances it was made in. Fo mysefl I would have cropped the top off, and tried to burn the hood of the car and the pole.  It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges.  CheersPaul', '2007-10-16 23:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
