(4190131, 594348, 66384, '<td valign="top">This is quite an amazing find. I have no idea what it is, but it certainly fits the challenge. To me, the grain makes it look all the more mysterious, and I think it is very good for the image. However, it probably wasn''t so good for your score. Regardless of what the voters said, I say "well done".</td>', 'This is quite an amazing find. I have no idea what it is, but it certainly fits the challenge. To me, the grain makes it look all the more mysterious, and I think it is very good for the image. However, it probably wasn''t so good for your score. Regardless of what the voters said, I say "well done".', '2007-10-23 18:08:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4190150, 594624, 66384, '<td valign="top">Wow, you have taken the leap into serious creativity -- creating the shot, I mean. This is really a good step for you, IMO. You were always good at spotting and capturing a good photo, and you have mastered PP. This will take the final restrictions off your ability to create art with your camera. I can''t wait for more of these.<br/> <br/>BTW, I think this is a great success. Excellent color, clarity, and composition.</td>', 'Wow, you have taken the leap into serious creativity -- creating the shot, I mean. This is really a good step for you, IMO. You were always good at spotting and capturing a good photo, and you have mastered PP. This will take the final restrictions off your ability to create art with your camera. I can''t wait for more of these. BTW, I think this is a great success. Excellent color, clarity, and composition.', '2007-10-23 18:16:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4190180, 593420, 66384, '<td valign="top">It does take some time to understand what this is. Once figured out, I totally appreciate it. I love the "automobile" and think you captured quite an appropriate dichotomy.</td>', 'It does take some time to understand what this is. Once figured out, I totally appreciate it. I love the "automobile" and think you captured quite an appropriate dichotomy.', '2007-10-23 18:32:57.000000', NULL, 0),
